%SIXMD 1
# @?INIT - START AND RESPAWN SYSTEM SERVICES

## @?OPTIONS

## @?OPERANDS

## DESCRIPTION

INIT IS THE FIRST USER PROCESS.  IT APPLIES STORAGE ACTIVATION POLICY FROM
/CONFIG/SYSTEM, FILESYSTEM MOUNT POLICY FROM /CONFIG/FSTAB, READS
/CONFIG/INITTAB, STARTS THE CONFIGURED SERVICES, WAITS FOR CHILDREN, AND
RESPAWNS ENTRIES MARKED FOR RESPAWN.

INIT MUST RUN AS PROCESS 1.

## @?FILES

### @?/CONFIG/SYSTEM
SYSTEM STORAGE POLICY READ AT STARTUP.  THE DEFAULT, INCLUDING WHEN THE FILE IS
ABSENT, IS:

SWAP = AUTO
LOGSTORE = AUTO

AUTO ENABLES A RESERVATION DISCOVERED BY KINIT; IF NO SUCH RESERVATION EXISTS,
BOOT CONTINUES WITHOUT THAT SERVICE.  OFF LEAVES THE SERVICE INACTIVE.  KINIT
STILL OWNS ROOT/STORAGE DISCOVERY AND RESIDENT SERVICE INSTALLATION; INIT OWNS
THE ADMINISTRATIVE ENABLE/OFF DECISION.  SWAP OFF ALSO DISABLES MEMFS SWAP
BACKING AND PERSISTENT MEMFS SNAPSHOT/RESTORE.  LOGSTORE OFF DISABLES NEW
LOGSTORE APPENDS.

### @?/CONFIG/FSTAB
FILESYSTEM MOUNT TABLE READ AT STARTUP.

FSTAB V1 ACCEPTS BLANK LINES, COMMENTS BEGINNING WITH #, AND MEMFS ENTRIES:

MEMFS:/EXISTING/MOUNT/POINT:WORDS
MEMFS:/EXISTING/MOUNT/POINT:WORDS:PERSIST

MEMFS IS A SINGLETON.  THE TARGET DIRECTORY MUST ALREADY EXIST.  WORDS IS THE
LOGICAL CAPACITY LIMIT; MUTABLE FILE DATA USES CORE ONLY WHILE RESIDENT.
PERSIST REQUESTS ORDERLY-HALT SNAPSHOT/RESTORE IN AN EXPLICIT PART OF THE SWAP
TAIL AND FAILS IF SUITABLE BACKING IS UNAVAILABLE.  ORDINARY MEMFS IS VOLATILE
AND CONTINUES TO WORK WITHOUT SWAP.

INIT EXPECTS /TEMP TO BE BACKED BY MEMFS AFTER MOUNTALL COMPLETES.  IF FSTAB
DOES NOT MOUNT MEMFS ON /TEMP, INIT PRINTS A WARNING AND CONTINUES BOOTING.
THIS IS INTENTIONAL ON THE 32K LOW-MEMORY PROFILE, WHICH LEAVES MEMFS
UNMOUNTED TO PRESERVE CORE.

### @?/CONFIG/INITTAB

ENTRIES HAVE THE FORM:

    TTY:ACTION:PROGRAM[:OUTPUT]

OUTPUT IS OPTIONAL.  NATIVE PRESERVES THE PHYSICAL TERMINAL'S NORMAL OUTPUT
PATH.  DPY KEEPS INPUT ON THE NAMED LOGICAL TERMINAL BUT SENDS ITS OUTPUT TO
THE TYPE-340 DISPLAY.  THIS PERMITS, FOR EXAMPLE, TTY0 TO USE THE CTY KEYBOARD
FOR LOGIN INPUT WHILE LOGIN AND THE RESULTING SESSION ARE DISPLAYED ON DPY.
SYSTEM SERVICE TABLE READ AT STARTUP.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?1 - STARTUP FAILED
INIT EXITS ONLY WHEN IT CANNOT RUN AS PROCESS 1 OR CANNOT LOAD ITS REQUIRED
STARTUP CONFIGURATION.
